        "available": {
          "description": "Admission against available host memory on top of the resident-set budget. Warden guard, warden danger and swap-out above the freeze threshold hold every start. Otherwise a unit starts when available memory is unknown or its predicted peak fits the available bytes less the margin and the unrealized share of running units. An idle broker with insufficient room starts one unit after the wait only while the warden is calm. A prior warden cancellation doubles the wait.",
          "marginBasisPoints": 1500,
          "waitMilliseconds": 180000,
          "pollMilliseconds": 1000,
          "cancelledFactorBasisPoints": 12500,
          "cancelledMemoryMilliseconds": 3600000
        },
        "unitCeiling": {
          "description": "The compile-memory budget per worker class: the most one compile unit may hold at its peak so that it fits the smallest worker (a 16 GB Mac that runs several agents). A library unit (everything but a `cdylib`) stays within `libraryMegabytes`; only a final `cdylib` link unit may use the higher `finalMegabytes`, and it must use the serial back end. `workerClass` names the class the fleet is carved for. `carving` is the closed list of units known to exceed their budget, each with its measured peak and the reduction it waits for; the list may only shrink. Every carving entry declares `budgetMegabytes`, the budget the host warden enforces at runtime for that unit (at least its measured peak, at most 10 percent above it): a unit on the list is cancelled while it runs once its resident footprint exceeds it; an unlisted unit is cancelled above the budget of its kind.",
          "workerClass": "16g",
          "classes": {
            "16g": {
              "hostMegabytes": 16384,
              "libraryMegabytes": 1536,
              "finalMegabytes": 4096,
              "finalBackend": "serial"
            }
